  "title": "The Eraser’s Overtime",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "creative-work struggles",
  "premise": "An illustrator wants a clean first line and erases every stroke until the paper becomes a transparent window. Looking through the hole reveals the messy sketch beneath, which already contains the desired pose; they trace only its strongest contour and let the rest stay loose.",
  "hook": "The eraser has done more work than the pencil.",
  "visible_action": "Pencil touches down; eraser scrubs; paper thins; lower sketch appears; one decisive contour closes around a pose.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "An imperfect attempt may contain the part you need.",
  "gate": "Magical paper erosion, no literal instruction to damage materials; not a universal creative method claim.",
